      ],
      "source": "https://kids.kiddle.co/Wingate,_Maryland",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Locals affectionately call Wingate the \"Heart of the Eastern Shore,\" a nickname that highlights its central position in the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://kids.kiddle.co/Wingate,_Maryland",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Wingate lies along Wingate Bishops Head Road, just northeast of the Honga River, a notable waterway in southern Dorchester County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wingate%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Because it is unincorporated, Wingate does not have its own mayor or city council; all local governance comes from the county.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        18,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://kids.kiddle.co/Wingate,_Maryland",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Dorchester County, where Wingate is located, boasts more shoreline than any other Maryland county, underscoring the area's maritime heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
